First Author: Zhu
Title: Construction and validation of a machine learning-based prediction model for venous thromboembolism in lung transplant recipients supported by ECMO
Source number: 77

Very short summary: This retrospective single-center study included 189 adult lung transplant recipients receiving postoperative ECMO at a Chinese hospital between May 2023 and November 2024. Six machine-learning algorithms were developed using six RFE-selected predictors; the Random Forest model was selected for temporal validation and achieved an AUC of 0.895 (95% CI 0.788–1.000), accuracy of 89.7%, sensitivity of 89.7%, and specificity of 89.5%.

